{
 "about": [
  "The shared fixture of the text fold (P2-25, audit B-37). Two test suites read THIS file and nothing else, so the server (Python, `textnorm.py`) and the phone (Dart, `text_fold.dart`) cannot disagree:",
  "server/encore_server/tests/test_textnorm.py and app/test/domain/text_fold_test.dart. A change to this folder runs both (server.yml and app.yml list it).",
  "The rows are written BY HAND from the design table (docs/tasks/P2-songs-as-references.md, P2-25 part 3): the expected values are never pasted from the code. The `corpus` section is the only generated part",
  "(`python -X utf8 tools/gen_text_fold_table.py`, with the Python 3.12 the server runs on): digests of the fold of every code point and of 20,000 seeded random strings; the algorithms are in",
  "server/encore_server/tests/textfold_corpus.py. A digest that differs means the fold changed: bump textnorm.TEXTNORM_REVISION, then rerun the tool. `revision` and `unidata_version` are written by hand, on purpose.",
  "Sections. fold: `input`, its `fold` (the character stage, punctuation kept), its `words`, its `key` (what key_text gives: the words joined, never empty when there is something to read).",
  "meet / differ: pairs whose keys must be equal / different; `a` and `b` are a text (compared by key_text) or [artist, title] (compared by the key `artist|title|`, which is what refs.norm_key gives from slice 2 on).",
  "survives: `era0` is textnorm.survives_fold_whole today (the form N-34 calls: decided against the old ASCII fold), `era1` is what it becomes when slice 2 merges (true for every text with a letter or a digit that the fold keeps).",
  "keys: [artist, title] and the full key `artist|title|version` (no bracket in any title, so the version is empty); the server tests it today with key_text and from slice 2 with refs.norm_key. The phone builds no keys.",
  "The phone checks fold and words (and meet and differ through them); `survives` and `keys` are server only."
 ],
